<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/plans-review.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/plans-review-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/plans-review.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/claim-math/">Claim math</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal File Strength Test</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist · runs in your browser</p><h1>Appraisal File Strength Test</h1><p class="lede">Answer twelve questions about your claim file. The score is weighted toward what appraisal panels rely on most, and every “no” becomes an item on your to-do list.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal file strength test</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied outright, talk with a Maine attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the carrier accepted coverage for at least part of the loss, in writing?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask the adjuster for the full itemized estimate, including the price list date and any photo report."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete line-item estimate, not just a summary page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an itemized estimate. A one-line contractor bid rarely holds up in front of an appraisal panel."><span>Do you have your own line-item estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Pull every photo and video you have, note the dates, and photograph current conditions now."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss, before snow, cleanup or repairs?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet insulation, sheathing and framing have been inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up: attic, wall cavities, subfloor, decking?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the Appraisal condition, note any deadlines for naming an appraiser, and check how umpire costs are shared."><span>Have you read the Appraisal paragraph in your policy’s conditions?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Locate the “Suit Against Us” condition and put the date on your calendar with the claim date tracker."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Finish reasonable mitigation and keep every receipt, invoice and fuel or rental bill."><span>Were temporary repairs made and receipts saved (tarps, water extraction, heat)?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request the current declarations page showing limits and deductibles."><span>Is your declarations page in hand?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect emails, letters and adjuster notes in date order in one folder."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run both numbers through the settlement gap projector; a narrow gap may be cheaper to close with a documented supplement."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, complete and return it before the stated deadline."><span>If the carrier asked for a sworn proof of loss, was it submitted on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Clear answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-score" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3e9f0" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e2683c" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Close these gaps first</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"><li>Nothing flagged yet.</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint fine">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and on your policy, and aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><h2>Why preparation comes first</h2>
<p>The award is binding on the amount of loss once two of the three panel members sign it. If a damaged area was never opened up, or your estimate is a single lump sum, it’s hard to add later. The strongest files have three things: accepted coverage, two itemized estimates, and dated proof of the damage.</p>
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, both itemized estimates and the carrier’s full estimate count most. Photos, hidden-damage inspection, policy reading and mitigation come next, then the paperwork that keeps a file organized.</p>
<ul><li><strong>75 or above:</strong> ready for a professional look at the dollar gap.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the flagged items first.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now risks a low award.</li></ul>
<p>Next steps: <a href="/the-appraisal-path/">the appraisal path, step by step</a>, or the <a href="/claim-math/settlement-gap-projector/">settlement gap projector</a>.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is a high score a prediction of the award?</summary><p>No. It measures how complete your file is, not the outcome. Pricing, policy terms and the facts of the loss decide the award.</p></details><details><summary>Why does coverage count so heavily?</summary><p>Appraisal resolves the amount of a covered loss. If coverage itself is denied, the dispute usually belongs with an attorney.</p></details><details><summary>Are my answers saved?</summary><p>No. Everything stays in your browser and clears when you close or reload the page.</p></details></div>
